From 74dd3bde2df71ea2da178031f2e49db3ff1cb2cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:35:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] IPv6 listeners (dual stack), per-/64 limiting and
 lockout, IPv6 ranges in limit_exempt/trusted_proxies

- bind accepts IPv6 (::1, specific address, :: = dual stack); IPv4-mapped peers reported as plain IPv4
- vdrx_iplimit: IPv4/IPv6 parse+format (RFC 5952), per-/64 limit key, 128-bit CIDR matcher
- WebSocket login lockout counted per /64
- DecodePeer unit-tested against kernel sockaddr layouts; ipv6 integration section (skips without IPv6)
- spawn fixture trusts 127.0.0.1 as proxy; edge-policy checks CGI-side forwarded headers
